/-- **ν and an optimal pose of `Johnson.TriaugmentedTruncatedDodecahedron.polyhedron` as one root**: when the representatives' systems have
exactly one root each, of scale `N`, the system `S` has exactly one root, of scale `N`, and at it
`matAt x 83`, `matAt x 74` and `(x 92, x 93)` are a weak fit of `Johnson.TriaugmentedTruncatedDodecahedron.polyhedron` scaled
by `N` through itself. -/
theorem johnsonTriaugmentedTruncatedDodecahedron_pose_of_reps {N : ℝ} (h : PolynomialSystem.IsRootEq [Pose.JohnsonTriaugmentedTruncatedDodecahedron.reps0, Pose.JohnsonTriaugmentedTruncatedDodecahedron.reps1] N) :
    PolynomialSystem.IsPoseRoot Johnson.TriaugmentedTruncatedDodecahedron.polyhedron Pose.JohnsonTriaugmentedTruncatedDodecahedron.S N 83 74 92 := by
  rw [Pose.JohnsonTriaugmentedTruncatedDodecahedron.S_eq]
  exact PolynomialSystem.ct_isPoseRoot h List.mem_cons_self Pose.JohnsonTriaugmentedTruncatedDodecahedron.len_eq Pose.JohnsonTriaugmentedTruncatedDodecahedron.reps_eq
    (Root.ParData.sqrt_spec (by decide +kernel)) Pose.JohnsonTriaugmentedTruncatedDodecahedron.par_ok Pose.JohnsonTriaugmentedTruncatedDodecahedron.zs_eq Pose.JohnsonTriaugmentedTruncatedDodecahedron.weak_ok Pose.JohnsonTriaugmentedTruncatedDodecahedron.poly_eq Pose.JohnsonTriaugmentedTruncatedDodecahedron.ok

end Nieuwland.Polyhedra
